  <h2 style="text-align:center;">Prime form of RCB</h2>
<p>The prime RCB was 2015-2016, and it was pure box-office cricket.

It was the only team in IPL history where you had *Virat Kohli - the Chase Machine*, *Chris Gayle - the Universe Boss*, and *Mr. 360 AB de Villiers* in the same top 3. If one didn't get you, the next one absolutely would.

Gayle would give you that terrifying start - 30 balls 60, just standing and dispatching. Then AB would walk in and do things that defied physics - scoops, reverse sweeps, 360-degree sixes that left bowlers clueless. And then there was Kohli in 2016, in the form of his life - 973 runs in a single season, 4 hundreds, chasing like a man possessed

That trio wasn't just batting, it was an event. Chinnaswamy would be shaking, 40,000 people chanting RCB-RCB, and any total under 200 felt 50 runs short. They didn't win the trophy then, but that team is why a whole generation still supports RCB - fearless, entertaining, and absolutely unstoppable on their day.</p>
